From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: give the input method the caret's place with on-the-spot input

Purpose: Japanese input shows the text being converted in the text box,
with the candidate window under it.
XP behavior: the IME draws the composition at the caret (or in the
application's composition window) and its candidate list under it.
Wine before: Wine asks for on-the-spot (callback) preedit, but sent the
place of the composition (XNSpotLocation) only with over-the-spot style,
so with on-the-spot fcitx5 showed its candidate window at the corner of
the window. (fcitx5 offers XIM clients on-the-spot only with its XIM
frontend's UseOnTheSpot option, which the win4wine session now sets.)
Change: with the opt-in, send the spot with on-the-spot style too, at the
bottom of the line, since the input method places its window under it.
Evidence: in the test VM with fcitx5 and Mozc, Notepad and XP's Run
dialog show the text inline and the candidates under the line.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL; over-the-spot is unchanged.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/xim.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/xim.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/xim.c
index bb227dc..b3eaf37 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/xim.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/xim.c
@@ -537,13 +537,20 @@ BOOL X11DRV_SetIMECompositionRect( HWND hwnd, RECT rect )
     XVaNestedList attr;
     XPoint xpoint;
 
-    if (!(input_style & XIMPreeditPosition))
+    /* win4wine: with on-the-spot (callbacks) the composition is drawn here,
+     * but the input method still places its candidate window at the spot */
+    if (!(input_style & XIMPreeditPosition) &&
+        !(win4wine_external_shell() && (input_style & XIMPreeditCallbacks)))
         return FALSE;
 
     if (!(data = get_win_data( hwnd ))) return FALSE;
 
     xpoint.x = rect.left - data->rects.visible.left;
     xpoint.y = rect.top - data->rects.visible.top;
+    /* win4wine: the input method places its candidate window under the spot,
+     * which for over-the-spot is the text's top; on-the-spot text is ours,
+     * so give the bottom of the line to keep the window off it */
+    if (!(input_style & XIMPreeditPosition)) xpoint.y = rect.bottom - data->rects.visible.top;
     if (!data->xic)
     {
         /* The XIC is made at the first key press or focus, often after the
